00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:37.170
So in this case, the evaluation metric plus the depth set, it prefers algorithm A

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:41.050
because the same look, algorithm A has lower error, which is the metric you're

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:49.010
using, but your U and your users prefer algorithm B because it's not letting

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:51.090
through pornographic images.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:56.410
So when this happens, when your evaluation metric is no longer correctly

00:01:56.410 --> 00:02:01.970
rank ordering preferences between algorithms, in this case, it's mispredicting

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:05.410
that algorithm A is a better algorithm, then that's a sign that you should

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:13.410
change your evaluation metric or perhaps your development set or test set.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:17.810
So in this case, the misclassification error metric that you're using can be

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:18.810
written as follows.

