00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:28.830
And if you want this normalization constant to still be right, technically

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:36.270
this becomes sum over i of wi, so then this error will still be between zero and 1.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:39.030
So the details of this weighting aren't important.

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:42.710
And to actually implement this weighting, you need to actually go through your

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:48.110
dev and test sets to label the pornographic images in your dev and test

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:50.990
sets so you can implement this weighting function.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:56.310
But the high level takeaway is if you find that your evaluation metric is not

00:04:56.310 --> 00:05:02.070
giving the correct rank order preference for what is actually a better algorithm,

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:07.590
then there's a time to think about defining a new evaluation metric that, you

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:11.350
know, and this is just one possible way that you could define a new evaluation

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:12.150
metric.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:15.710
But the goal of the evaluation metric is to accurately tell you, given two

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:20.550
class i's, which one is better for your application.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:23.510
For the purpose of this video, don't worry too much about the details of how

