we define a new error metric.

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:29.350
The point is that if you're not satisfied with your own error metric,

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:33.150
then don't keep coasting with an error metric you're unsatisfied with.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:37.350
Instead, try to define a new one that you think better captures your preferences

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.870
in terms of what's actually a better algorithm.

